        "draft": "Blackthorn reaches into a fold of her aubergine suit and produces a worn pair of leather boots, offering them with a businesslike tilt of her head. \"On the house,\" she says, her nearly black eyes sliding over Nicco's visible white hairs without comment. \"Consider it an opening favor. I'm Blackthorn—I handle arrangements for certain parties who need things moved, housed, or otherwise managed.\"\n\nShe turns slightly, glancing toward the Tower's heavy wooden entrance, then back to Nicco. \"Heartstone's been empty longer than I've been in this district. Guessing you're why that changed.\" Her voice carries no particular warmth, just the brisk patience of someone who dislikes wasted time. \"If you're settling in and need supplies, labor, or information about who's who in the neighborhood, I trade in all three. Fair rates. No complications unless you bring them.\"",
